1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,000
Did you sell out Uvo?

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Answer me!

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,000
[thunder crashing]

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:13,000
[Nobunaga] I'll take that as a yes.

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Move!

6
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Now, hold on a minute.
Let's hear what he has to say.

7
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Are you kidding?
What's there to say?

8
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Just calm down, alright?
Remember what the boss said.

9
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:26,000
There are ways we can avoid the events
that are predicted in the fortune.

10
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Hisoka, explain to us
what happened this week.

11
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,000
[Hisoka] I cannot.

12
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Huh?

13
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:37,000
Sorry, but all that I can tell you
is that the first poem was accurate.

14
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Nothing more, I'm afraid.

15
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:44,000
-Do you hear that? Move!
-Wait. Not just yet.

16
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Hisoka, why can't you explain?

17
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Because telling you would amount
to saying what I cannot.

18
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:52,000
So, I say nothing.

19
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:55,000
But it's not that I won't tell,

20
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,000
it's that I can't say more
than I already have.

21
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:02,000
If you won't accept that answer,

22
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:05,000
then for the sake of defending myself...

23
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:08,000
I have no other choice but to fight.

24
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:12,000
[theme music playing]

25
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:33,000
ALLIES x AND x LIES

26
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:36,000
[narrator] After seeing his fortune,

27
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:39,000
Nobunaga suspects Hisoka
has betrayed them,

28
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:41,000
and draws his sword.

29
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:51,000
[scoffs] Forget it.
You're way too much of a pain to fight.

30
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:55,000
Yeah right! Like that would stop me!

31
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:58,000
[gasps]

32
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:02,000
[Chrollo] Nobunaga.

33
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:06,000
-Be quiet a moment.
-Huh?

34
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:10,000
-Did the boss just do that?
-Probably.

35
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:15,000
Hisoka, I have some questions for you.

36
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:17,000
Answer them if you can.

37
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:22,000
In the fortune, tell me,
what does "secrets" mean?

38
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:24,000
[Hisoka] The Troupe members' powers.

39
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:26,000
[Chrollo] How many of them?

40
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:30,000
Seven. No, excuse me, eight.

41
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:35,000
You and Uvogin, Shizuku, Machi, Franklin,

42
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:38,000
Pakunoda, Shalnark and I make eight.

43
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:43,000
Hmm. You only learned
of Kortopi's ability yesterday?

44
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:45,000
[Hisoka] That's correct.

45
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:48,000
-What's the chain-user's ability?
-Can't say.

46
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:51,000
-Can you say what he looks like?
-I cannot.

47
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:54,000
And what is your relationship to him?

48
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:56,000
I can't tell you.

49
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:00,000
I understand.

50
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:05,000
BANDIT'S SECRET

51
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:12,000
The red-eyed customer is the chain user,
who possesses no fewer than two abilities.

52
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:16,000
The one that he used to capture Uvogin,

53
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:20,000
and the other is one
that restricts Hisoka's actions.

54
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:25,000
The "sword of law," the phrase mentioned
in the second poem of the fortune

55
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:28,000
forces a person to obey a set of rules.

56
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:31,000
Such as "don't lie to me."

57
00:04:32,000 --> 00:04:34,000
Or "do not reveal anything about me."

58
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:36,000
Something of that nature.

59
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:39,000
And it would also stand to reason

60
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:42,000
that he planted something
that's inside of Hisoka's body.

61
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:44,000
[chuckles]

62
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:49,000
The poem starts by mentioning
a trade of sorts,

63
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:52,000
but the second half just describes
what the customer took.

64
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:56,000
And this would seem to suggest
that the sword of law

65
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:58,000
was used to attack Hisoka.

66
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:03,000
In other words, Hisoka was forced
to betray us against his will.

67
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:06,000
[Hisoka] Oh, so good.

68
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:12,000
If the sword can curb Hisoka's speech,
it must be quite powerful indeed.

69
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:16,000
[Hisoka] Yes, I knew you were brilliant.

70
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:20,000
I'm definitely going to enjoy...
killing you.

71
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:22,000
Now, let's all review what we know.

72
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:25,000
First off, the enemy uses chains.

73
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:29,000
A Manipulator would be using
actual physical chains in battle.

74
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:33,000
If he's a Conjurer, then he took down Uvo
by using Nen chains.

75
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:35,000
So is there a difference
between those two?

76
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:39,000
[Shalnark] Yes, a big one.
A Conjurer can appear to be empty-handed.

77
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:42,000
That's a huge advantage.

78
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:43,000
I see.

79
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:46,000
Conjurers have to do lots
of visual training,

80
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:49,000
but once they have, they can make
their weapons appear at will.

81
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:53,000
But our real problem at the moment
is what's restricting Hisoka.

82
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:57,000
[Franklin] A sword of law must involve
rules he has to follow.

83
00:05:57,000 --> 00:06:01,000
[Shalnark] Yes, he's probably forced
to follow the orders Chrollo talked about.

84
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:04,000
He's likely barred
from attacking the chain user, as well.

85
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:07,000
And he would probably die
if he broke his promise.

86
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:11,000
[Hisoka chuckling] How fun.

87
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:15,000
There's no sword of law
anywhere in my body.

88
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:19,000
That fortune was my own creation.

89
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:24,000
I only revealed the abilities
of two members, not eight.

90
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:30,000
It was a risky gamble, one that would
have turned the entire Troupe against me

91
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:32,000
had the boss not figured that out.

92
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:37,000
All this to keep the spiders
in Yorknew City,

93
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:39,000
so I can fight the boss.

94
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:46,000
If they were to leave now,
there's no telling when I'd see him again.

95
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:52,000
But then what is Hisoka's second poem
supposed to mean?

96
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:56,000
It says "The 11-legged spider
longs for home.

97
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:59,000
Five more legs shall break
before it's done.

98
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:04,000
But from your shelter do not roam,
for of those five, you shall be one."

99
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:10,000
Our hideout. That's the temporary shelter.
If Hisoka leaves here, he'll die.

100
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:13,000
What about the longing for home?

101
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:15,000
It means that we're homesick.

102
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:18,000
[Shalnark] But if we do go back home,
then half of us won't survive.

103
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:20,000
Okay, I get it.

104
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:24,000
Uvo, Hisoka, Shizuku, Pakunoda
and Shalnark.

105
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:27,000
One more makes half the members.

106
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:30,000
Did the fortune predict any other deaths?

107
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:33,000
It has to be Feitan, Kortopi or me.

108
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:37,000
We didn't have all the data we needed
to get our fortunes told.

109
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:40,000
I'm staying right here for the time being.

110
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:43,000
There are things that I still wish to do
before I die.

111
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:46,000
I won't be leaving our shelter.

112
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:50,000
Well, boss, what now?

113
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:52,000
[Phinks] Leave or stay?

114
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:04,000
[Chrollo] Let's stay.

115
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:07,000
[Killua] No way.

116
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:10,000
Wait, but why not? You were the one
who wanted to go and capture

117
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:12,000
the Phantom Troupe in the first place.

118
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:14,000
Yeah, well that was back when it wouldn't
have been pointless.

119
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:16,000
But why is it pointless?

120
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:18,000
'Cause there's no reward money anymore,

121
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:21,000
so you would be taking
a huge risk for absolutely nothing.

122
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:26,000
Maybe so, but it'd be worth it to finally
capture the Phantom Troupe, wouldn't it?

123
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:29,000
You really need to take a hard look
at your priorities.

124
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:32,000
Do you even remember why we're here?
Well, do you?

125
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:35,000
-For Greed Island.
-Exactly!

126
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:38,000
The Southern Piece auction
starts in two days,

127
00:08:38,000 --> 00:08:41,000
so we need to make a whole lot
of money before then.

128
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:44,000
Actually, I have a great idea
about how we can get the game.

129
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:46,000
You've got a plan, fill me in.

130
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:50,000
Hmm. It's a secret right now!

131
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:53,000
[groaning] Stop being such a little tease
and spit it out!

132
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:56,000
I can't breathe! You're gonna kill me!

133
00:08:57,000 --> 00:09:00,000
Anyway, I'll figure out something
for the game, but for now,

134
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:02,000
we should keep trailing the Troupe.

135
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:05,000
Do you really have a plan
to get Greed Island?

136
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:08,000
Yeah, but it isn't guaranteed to work
or anything.

137
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:11,000
Well, okay then, how likely is it to work?

138
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:14,000
Like, what's the probability of success?

139
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:17,000
Uh, maybe 70 percent.

140
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:22,000
-Seventy?
-I mean, maybe more like 60.

141
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:26,000
[Killua] So, it's probably 50-50.

142
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:29,000
But still, I guess that’s a lot better

143
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:32,000
than trying to earn six billion Jenny
in two days.

144
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:34,000
[Killua] Okay, fine.

145
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:36,000
I'll let you be in charge of Greed Island,

146
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:40,000
but it'd be stupid to try to deal
with the Troupe on our own.

147
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:44,000
We'll need Kurapika's help.
We can't do this without him.

148
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:45,000
Hmm.

149
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:49,000
[Melody] Where are you off to, boss?

150
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:52,000
I'm going shopping.
I told you that earlier, didn't I?

151
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:57,000
[Melody] Basho and I will accompany you.
You okay here, Squala?

152
00:09:57,000 --> 00:09:58,000
No problem.

153
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:01,000
[Squala] That was close!

154
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:04,000
[Melody]
Guard those Scarlet Eyes well, alright?

155
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:07,000
Sure. As long as these guys are here,
I should be fine.

156
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:10,000
[dogs whining]

157
00:10:11,000 --> 00:10:12,000
[Melody] Okay, I'm off.

158
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:15,000
[Squala] Yeah, I'll see you later.

159
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:23,000
[footsteps approaching]

160
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:24,000
How did it go?

161
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:26,000
I couldn't get a straight answer.

162
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:31,000
I asked the community for any updates
regarding the auction today, but no luck.

163
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:34,000
You should go back there and tell them
the Troupe is still alive!

164
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:37,000
That ought to make them
change their minds.

165
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:40,000
I'm afraid that still
won't change anything.

166
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:43,000
The Mafia wants to avoid any friction
with Meteor City.

167
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:47,000
I think it's safe to assume that their war
on the Phantom Troupe is over.

168
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:49,000
Really?

169
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:52,000
But that wasn't the information
I was hoping to find.

170
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:57,000
My only real concern is whether
the auction will proceed as planned.

171
00:10:57,000 --> 00:11:00,000
Are you thinking of intercepting them?

172
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:03,000
That's insane!

173
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:07,000
How do you think you're gonna do that
without the Mafia's help, huh?

174
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:09,000
You have it all wrong, Leorio.

175
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:13,000
I'm not counting on the Mafia.
Far from it.

176
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:14,000
[gasps]

177
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:18,000
[Gon]
Hey, Kurapika, let us help you, okay?

178
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:21,000
We'll do anything.
Just tell us what you need.

179
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:23,000
[Killua] Come on, say no.

180
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:27,000
-But the reward was rescinded.
-[Gon] I know.

181
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:30,000
I still want to stop the Troupe.
I haven't changed my mind about that.

182
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:34,000
[Killua] Turn him down.
Turn him down!

183
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:36,000
You'd be risking your lives.

184
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:40,000
[Killua]
Great. Throw a little fuel on the fire.

185
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:46,000
Right. Then let's discuss it.

186
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:47,000
Okay.

187
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:48,000
[Killua] He agreed?

188
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:52,000
First, we're gonna need someone
to watch their base

189
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:54,000
and to provide updates.

190
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:55,000
Yeah, I can do that.

191
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:58,000
[Kurapika] We only want the woman
called Pakunoda.

192
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:01,000
-You can ignore the others.
-Okay.

193
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:03,000
Be incredibly careful.

194
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:05,000
Oh, don't worry. I won't push my luck.

195
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:08,000
I'm also going to need a driver
to accompany me.

196
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:10,000
Leorio, can I count on you?

197
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:13,000
[spluttering] Yeah.

198
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:14,000
It'll be fine.

199
00:12:15,000 --> 00:12:17,000
You'll be totally safe
if you're with Kurapika.

200
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:18,000
[Leorio] Oh, knock it off, Killua.

201
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:22,000
You're making it sound like I'm terrified
or something, and I'm totally not!

202
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:23,000
Okay, what about me?

203
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:26,000
[Kurapika] Create a diversion
that will draw their focus.

204
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:31,000
Hey, wait a minute!
That job sounds way too dangerous.

205
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:34,000
You really expect Gon
to face the Troupe members again?

206
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:36,000
[Kurapika] Depends on our strategy.

207
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:38,000
I'm listening. What kind of strategy?

208
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:40,000
A simple one, actually.

209
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:42,000
While the enemy is busy dealing with Gon,

210
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:45,000
I'll capture Pakunoda
and quietly make my escape.

211
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:48,000
That plan sounds a little shaky to me.

212
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:50,000
[Kurapika]
Perhaps, but there are too many variables

213
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:52,000
to devise anything more concrete.

214
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:56,000
Now, as for Gon's strategy,
I'll let him decide that.

215
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:58,000
Just hold their attention
for at least half a second,

216
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:00,000
a full second if possible.

217
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:02,000
A full second, if I can?

218
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:03,000
[Kurapika] Yes.

219
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:07,000
[Gon]
Keep their attention for a whole second?

220
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:10,000
Can I do that?

221
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:13,000
[Kurapika] Gon.

222
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:15,000
You're the key to this plan.
Can you handle it?

223
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:19,000
I'm not really sure. I need time to think.

224
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:21,000
We have six hours.

225
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:24,000
If the auction proceeds as scheduled...

226
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:28,000
the spiders will make their move
before then.

227
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:35,000
Hey, you never let us help you before.
Why start now?

228
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:40,000
Because the risk I'm taking has grown.
I must eliminate Pakunoda immediately.

229
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:42,000
No matter the cost.

230
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:45,000
[Killua gasps] Wow.

231
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:49,000
[Leorio] So, this is why Kurapika
seems so different.

232
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:51,000
His resolve's gotten even stronger.

233
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:54,000
Kurapika.

234
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:57,000
Could you use your Nen dagger on me?

235
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:00,000
-[gasps]
-What are you talking about?

236
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:03,000
Yeah, weren't you listening?

237
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:06,000
If Kurapika attacks someone who's not
a Spider, he'll die!

238
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:07,000
Keep your voice down!

239
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:12,000
Then I don't get it. Kurapika has
a Nen dagger in his chest, doesn't he?

240
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:13,000
[gasping]

241
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:16,000
I mean, since he's not a member
of the Phantom Troupe...

242
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:23,000
What I'm about to say
will make the risk I face even greater.

243
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:26,000
Okay.

244
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:30,000
Let's go, Killua.

245
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:47,000
The answer to your question is yes.
It's possible.

246
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:52,000
Each of my five chains has a separate
and unique function.

247
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:57,000
And two of them are to be used
solely against the Spiders.

248
00:14:58,000 --> 00:15:00,000
This one is Chain Jail.

249
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:04,000
It restrains the target and forces them
into a state of Zetsu.

250
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:07,000
This is for capturing Spiders.

251
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:13,000
This one is called Judgment Chain.

252
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:19,000
I stab the target's heart with this dagger
and declare a binding rule.

253
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:22,000
Break that rule and you die.

254
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:29,000
As you're aware, there's a Nen dagger
residing in my own heart, as well.

255
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:34,000
At first, I planned to use it on myself
on the condition that I would die

256
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:37,000
if I ever used my chains
against anyone outside the Troupe.

257
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:41,000
But then I realized
I had missed something.

258
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:45,000
What if attacking myself meant breaking
the very rule I had set?

259
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:47,000
[thunder crashing]

260
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:53,000
It was possible I would be an exception,

261
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:56,000
but there was no way for me
to know for sure.

262
00:15:56,000 --> 00:15:58,000
So, I adjusted the rule further.

263
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:03,000
I will only use my Chain Jail
against the Phantom Troupe.

264
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:08,000
That means I can use Judgment Chain
on anyone I choose.

265
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:12,000
But that chain has a condition too.

266
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:14,000
But what kind of condition?

267
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:19,000
[Kurapika] This chain can only be used
when my eyes are scarlet.

268
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:22,000
Hey, wait. You can change them yourself?

269
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:24,000
It took practice.

270
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:27,000
It was a while before I could turn them
scarlet at will.

271
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:34,000
I mastered the power in my middle finger
by vowing never to release the chain

272
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:36,000
and to always risk death.

273
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:41,000
The one in my little finger was resolved
by my unique nature.

274
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:45,000
When my eyes turn scarlet
is when I become a Specialist.

275
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:50,000
And I gain the ability to use
any power I've learned at full strength.

276
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:56,000
I'm not sure what all that means,

277
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:59,000
but what about your Nen dagger?
You can use it on me, can't you?

278
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:01,000
Yes.

279
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:05,000
Go ahead. Set whatever rule you want.

280
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:10,000
You're dedicated. I appreciate that.

281
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:14,000
Just curious. Can you make three
of those daggers?

282
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:16,000
You can just cancel it, right?

283
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:18,000
Erase the rule as soon
as the mission's over?

284
00:17:18,000 --> 00:17:19,000
Killua! Leorio!

285
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:22,000
Killua and I had a little talk.

286
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:26,000
-And since we're working together...
-[Killua] We should risk together.

287
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:28,000
[Killua and Leorio] What do you say?

288
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:33,000
The answer to both is yes.

289
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:36,000
But all three of you
are making a big mistake.

290
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:40,000
I want you to know,
I never had any intention

291
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:42,000
of using my dagger on you guys.

292
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:47,000
Well, then why did you put yourself
in danger by telling us your secret?

293
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:49,000
[Kurapika] I wanted to thank you, Gon.

294
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:53,000
No, I wanted to thank all of you
for your resolve.

295
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:58,000
And if one of you ends up
revealing my secret, which I doubt,

296
00:17:58,000 --> 00:18:00,000
I still won't regret a thing.

297
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:07,000
I have been blessed with good friends.

298
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:15,000
That's not fair, Kurapika.

299
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:18,000
Because the pressure of risking my life

300
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:20,000
isn't nearly as bad
as letting down a friend.

301
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:24,000
That was my goal from the beginning.

302
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:27,000
Oh, okay! I get it now! [laughing]

303
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:29,000
[Kurapika chuckling]

304
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:31,000
[Killua] That is so not funny!

305
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:34,000
Alright.

306
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:38,000
Well, I'm heading out.
There's no time to waste.

307
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:40,000
Be real careful out there, Killua!

308
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:43,000
Yeah. You just leave it to me.

309
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:48,000
[thunder rumbling]

310
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:55,000
[Shizuku] In the chamber
of treasure ill-gotten,

311
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:58,000
there is no choice but endless sleep.

312
00:18:59,000 --> 00:19:04,000
Your greatest fear should solitude be,
lest upon your lonesome form he creep.

313
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:09,000
[Pakunoda]
On a day dark and poorly lit,

314
00:19:09,000 --> 00:19:13,000
a simple choice: betrayal or pride.

315
00:19:13,000 --> 00:19:16,000
In a cramped room, you must face it.

316
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:19,000
For the reaper lingers at your side.

317
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:27,000
[Shalnark] Even one call do not make.
When needed most, it won't connect.

318
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:31,000
To answer your phone, another mistake.

319
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:34,000
One time in three,
the reaper calls collect.

320
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:37,000
Now, let's split up into groups.

321
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:40,000
That's how we'll operate
for the next week.

322
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:43,000
Make absolutely sure you're never alone.

323
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:47,000
Shizuku, Pakunoda and Machi.

324
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:51,000
Kortopi, Phinks and Feitan.

325
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:55,000
Nobunaga and Shalnark are with me.

326
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:59,000
Bonolenov, Franklin
and Hisoka will stay here.

327
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:02,000
Hey, boss, just so you know...

328
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:05,000
Some little kids,
they know about this place.

329
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:06,000
[Chrollo] Kids?

330
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:09,000
Well, they don't have anything
to do with the chain user,

331
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:12,000
but I can't help but be
a little bit worried.

332
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:14,000
Oh, yeah, I totally forgot!

333
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:17,000
Hey boss, I think we ought to recruit
these kids.

334
00:20:17,000 --> 00:20:21,000
[Machi] Whoa, hold on. That wasn't
why I mentioned them, Nobunaga.

335
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:23,000
What do you mean?

336
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:29,000
[Chrollo] I see.
They do sound rather interesting.

337
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:34,000
But from what you've told me,
it doesn't sound like they'll join us.

338
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:37,000
Then we'll change their minds.
It's worth meeting them, at least.

339
00:20:37,000 --> 00:20:40,000
[Machi] No, boss, don't listen to him.

340
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:43,000
Alright, Machi, what is the source
of your concern?

341
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:46,000
It's... just a hunch.

342
00:20:46,000 --> 00:20:50,000
A hunch? Your instincts are too reliable
to ignore.

343
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:54,000
It could be there's something important
about those kids.

344
00:20:57,000 --> 00:21:00,000
Let's make more dummy hideouts
just to be safe.

345
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:03,000
Kortopi, can you make me ten more?

346
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:05,000
I can make 50.

347
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:09,000
And the second anyone enters
one of the fakes, I'll know.

348
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:13,000
See, my copies act as my En, too.

349
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:23,000
[Killua] Something's not right.
Am I in the wrong place?

350
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:25,000
No, that's impossible.

351
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:28,000
No way!

352
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:31,000
There weren't this many buildings before!

353
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:33,000
[thunder crashing]

354
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:46,000
[narrator] As rain falls, the operation
to capture Pakunoda begins.

355
00:21:47,000 --> 00:21:50,000
[theme music playing]

356
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:58,000
-[Gon] Coming up, Gon...
-[Killua] And Killua's...

357
00:22:58,000 --> 00:22:59,000
[both] Hunterpedia!

358
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:01,000
-I'm Gon!
-I'm Killua!

359
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:03,000
[both] And this is our Hunterpedia!

360
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:06,000
Today, we're introducing Feitan,
another Troupe member.

361
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:08,000
His hobby is torture,
which is pretty awesome.

362
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:10,000
[darkly] And he's interested
in Greed Island too.

363
00:23:11,000 --> 00:23:12,000
That's a pretty terrible impression.

364
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:20,000
[Gon] Next time:
"Beloved and Beleaguered."

365
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:22,000
-[Killua] Shepherd.
-[Gon] Woof!

366
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:23,000
-[Killua] Maltese.
-[Gon] Woof!

367
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:25,000
-[Killua] Pomeranian.
-[Gon] Woof!

368
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:27,000
-[Killua] Gon.
-[Gon] Hi!
